\newcommand{\ROBArduinoStatus}{%
  \begin{fieldnotebox}[title={ONE CURRENT ARDUINO, THREE HISTORICAL SKETCHES}]
  The \texttt{ROBArduino} archive preserves Base, Torso, and Head sketches from an earlier three-Arduino design. The builder reports that present-day ROB uses \textbf{only the Base sketch}. This book therefore treats Base behavior as the current low-level firmware reference and labels Torso and Head behavior as retired historical evidence. Source files cannot prove which binary is flashed today; record the board identity, firmware hash, build environment, and upload date before operation.
  \end{fieldnotebox}
}

\newcommand{\ROBAmberStatus}{%
  \begin{fieldnotebox}[title={TWO AMBER B1 ARMS, ONE DOCUMENTED CONTROL CHAIN}]
  ROB carries two seven-joint AMBER B1 arms. The repository snapshot separates their Ubuntu-side cores as \texttt{L-10} and \texttt{R-11}: network clients use UDP or LCM, each core binds a stable CAN interface, and CAN carries commands and feedback between that core and its arm actuators. The \texttt{AmberHomeFolder} tree is evidence from one Ubuntu machine, not a deployable image; never copy its credentials, logs, virtual environment, or machine-specific identifiers. Volume 6 documents the inspected protocol, URDF models, reproducible setup, verification gates, and unresolved configuration differences.
  \end{fieldnotebox}
}

\newcommand{\ROBSourceRoot}{%
  \begin{fieldnotebox}[title={HOW TO FIND THE FILES}]
  Open the public repositories on GitHub and follow each printed repository-relative path: \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBBooks}, \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBArduino}, \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/Cerebro}, \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBController}, \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBControllerVision}, \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/Amber-HomeFolder}, and \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBTrainingGames}. The website is published separately at \url{https://github.com/OrbitusRoboticsWebSite/ORobotics}. See \url{https://github.com/RudyAramayo/ROBBooks/blob/main/ROB-Books/OPEN-SOURCE-CODE-MAP.md} for clickable repository and file links, license cautions, and renamed-file search instructions. A named archival item without a verified public repository is labeled as evidence, not given an invented URL.
  \end{fieldnotebox}
}

